{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125845-the-author-of-this-grimoire-goes-by-my-name","id":1125845,"title":"\"The author of this Grimoire goes by... my name?\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-07T04:50:43-07:00","id":1125845,"title":"\"The author of this Grimoire goes by... my name?\"","content":"So your character finds a Grimoire which perfectly matches their paradigm and has concepts written in it that really resonate with you. It's a Grimoire that's potent enough to push up your Arete and your favourite Spheres. The author? You, at least according to the book. Its resonance matches yours; if someone were to investigate with Prime it would match up with your personal Quintessence signature almost perfectly.<br /> <br /> How are you explaining this? What's your theory? How would you investigate it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-07-2017, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T05:10:30-07:00","id":1125850,"title":"","content":"The same way you investigate everything else - give it to a time mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T05:17:51-07:00","id":1125854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125845-the-author-of-this-grimoire-goes-by-my-name?p=1125850#post1125850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same way you investigate everything else - give it to a time mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Infuriatingly, someone with a lot of time on their hands has taken steps to eliminate all Time-related traces from the book. Not only has it been scrubbed clean of its history and past impressions made by those who have touched it, it seems to have been scrubbed clean of a temporal nature of any kind. Dating when it was published, and when the notes were made, seems impossible using Time Magick. Your Time-adept friend grows frustrated and gives the book back to you, surmising that someone with a mastery of Time superior to theirs has been very careful in covering their tracks.<br /> <br /> (Side Note I promise this isn't a &quot;aaaaaaaaaand you fail&quot; it's actually a sort of clue for my personal explanation, however I can think of three good ones)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T07:16:02-07:00","id":1125893,"title":"","content":"Without nailing my temporary character down to a specific paradigm, I would have several explanations, depending;<br /> <br /> First, two premises:<br /> <br /> a) The Grimoire is just that - a Grimoire. It does what it's supposed to do<br /> <br /> b) It's a Trap! Custom-tailored for me, to be lured into safety by the resonance. And of course by somebody powerful. There is something nasty, hidden deep inside with double meanings and very carefully hidden effects. It might even do everything the Grimoire is promising to do, but there might be a..price..to pay, later. Or Instantly.<br /> <br /> Given those two, let's get to the origin:<br /> <br /> * It was indeed written by me in the future, and somehow made its way back. On purpose? No idea. Did I send it back? No idea.<br /> <br /> * The nature of the Grimoire's appearance might not involve Time at all. It might come from a parallel timeline/Everett Volume. How it got here? No idea. But a second me wrote it in a parallel plane.<br /> <br /> * The Grimoire was written by somebody else, but they took a LOT of time and investment to fake my resonance all over it, and mimic my writing.<br /> <br /> BONUS ENDING:<br /> * The Grimoire actually wasn't written by me, or any other Mage. Not really. Kind of. It comes from the High Umbra, one of the endless worlds where every concept that can exist, does exist - including the concept of a Grimoire written by me. How it got here? No idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T07:28:13-07:00","id":1125901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125845-the-author-of-this-grimoire-goes-by-my-name?p=1125893#post1125893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without nailing my temporary character down to a specific paradigm, I would have several explanations, depending;<br /> <br /> First, two premises:<br /> <br /> a) The Grimoire is just that - a Grimoire. It does what it's supposed to do<br /> <br /> b) It's a Trap! Custom-tailored for me, to be lured into safety by the resonance. And of course by somebody powerful. There is something nasty, hidden deep inside with double meanings and very carefully hidden effects. It might even do everything the Grimoire is promising to do, but there might be a..price..to pay, later. Or Instantly.<br /> <br /> Given those two, let's get to the origin:<br /> <br /> * It was indeed written by me in the future, and somehow made its way back. On purpose? No idea. Did I send it back? No idea.<br /> <br /> * The nature of the Grimoire's appearance might not involve Time at all. It might come from a parallel timeline/Everett Volume. How it got here? No idea. But a second me wrote it in a parallel plane.<br /> <br /> * The Grimoire was written by somebody else, but they took a LOT of time and investment to fake my resonance all over it, and mimic my writing.<br /> <br /> BONUS ENDING:<br /> * The Grimoire actually wasn't written by me, or any other Mage. Not really. Kind of. It comes from the High Umbra, one of the endless worlds where every concept that can exist, does exist - including the concept of a Grimoire written by me. How it got here? No idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good! This is practically every eventuality I considered. Potent demonic being that wants to lure you into service? Possible. You from the future? Possible. You from another world? Possible. Hadn't thought about the High Umbra, good point. Another Mage trying to attack you, possibly a Nephandi who wants to layer in some subtle Mind effects (couching anti-existence sentiment in ideas VERY similar to your own to make it more palatable; with me it would be ideas that run contrary to existence which bemoan that existence is suffering... my beliefs are based around the idea of promoting pleasure, and &quot;my own voice&quot; telling me that life is mostly suffering and that there's no way to achieve &quot;mass ascension&quot; through pleasure might be enough...)? Possible.<br /> <br /> A Cheap one is that it's all a Mind effect and everything about the Grimoire's power is a potent mental illusion, but it's a bit &quot;it was all a dream&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T07:43:18-07:00","id":1125905,"title":"","content":"(BTW does anyone know the rules for Grimoires? Like I'm thinking that it subtracts an EXP cost equal to its level from the things it can teach, so a level 5 Grimoire can teach up to Arete 5 and can teach 5 dots worth of Spheres (say Forces 5, or Correspondence 3, Matter 2, just has to add up to 5), and everything you learn within that scope has 5 EXP subtracted from it... only works if your Paradigm is in line with it of course, plus not having to do a Seeking removes a huge risk from leveling up Arete)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T07:45:38-07:00","id":1125907,"title":"","content":"Well, the fact that it's been purposely scrubbed of any temporal resonance implies that something interesting temporally was going on, and supports the theory that it came from the future or an alternate timeline - even if your Time friend can't prove it.<br /> <br /> You could look for sympathetic links, but those have probably been scrubbed too. You could awaken the spirit of the grimoire and interrogate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T07:50:19-07:00","id":1125909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125845-the-author-of-this-grimoire-goes-by-my-name?p=1125907#post1125907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could awaken the spirit of the grimoire and interrogate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spirit has been sworn to silen-<br /> <br /> Sorry ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T07:53:11-07:00","id":1125910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125845-the-author-of-this-grimoire-goes-by-my-name?p=1125907#post1125907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the fact that it's been purposely scrubbed of any temporal resonance implies that something interesting temporally was going on, and supports the theory that it came from the future or an alternate timeline - even if your Time friend can't prove it.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I did intend this as a hint, it's also worth nothing that ANYONE who wanted to give a mysterious object to a group of Mages without them figuring out it's origins would scrub the Temporal resonance. A good Master of Time can see everything that ever happened to the object (similar to Auspex 3, The Spirit's Touch) and that can scupper most plans. So a Nephandi using the book as a trojan horse for world-ending ideas via Mind would want to scrub it clean with Time... extra easy with the destructive alt-Spheres of the Nephandi, erasing resonance would be much easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T09:10:59-07:00","id":1125925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125845-the-author-of-this-grimoire-goes-by-my-name?p=1125905#post1125905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(BTW does anyone know the rules for Grimoires?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Official M20 rules from the Book Of Secrets are, that a Grimoire can help you raise an ability (or several), A sphere (or several), or Arete. Or a combination of those.<br /> <br /> What it does is, indeed, cut down the costs.<br /> <br /> Abilities: Half cost, though usually Grimoires focus on knowledges and esoteric specialties, rarely Talents or the like.<br /> Sphere: Current Rating x7, minus the grimoire's level in XP Grimoire's level is the Sphere limit.<br /> Affinity: Current Rating x6, minus the grimoire's level in XP. Grimoire's level is the Sphere limit.<br /> Arete: As usual, but no seeking is required. Arete can't raise over the Grimoire's level this way.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> &quot;Individual Grimoires may have other benefits, depending<br /> upon the book in question. The reader may gain only one<br /> benefit per reading, and may expand her Arete only once with<br /> a given Grimoire. A reader can benefit only once per year from<br /> a given Grimoire.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-07-2017, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T09:59:21-07:00","id":1125943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125845-the-author-of-this-grimoire-goes-by-my-name?p=1125925#post1125925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A reader can benefit only once per year from a given Grimoire.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I was nodding along reading this until this bit. I understand having to invest weeks of reading, make Intelligence + Academics or Wits + Esoterica or Perception + Research etc. needing to RP it through, but simply saying &quot;only one use per year&quot; feels silly. What if I use it to raise my Occult from 1 to 2? Is that it for a year? Feels idiotic. Also, can I use Time and Mind to accelerate my mind forward a year in terms of &quot;mental age&quot;, waiting outside of time with a fun project, to pop back a second later with a &quot;year&quot; having passed? Why a year? What's the justification or reason for this?<br /> <br /> If I play Mage I'm either going to use a kinder mechanic here so the Background is worth something OR ask the ST nicely haha.<br /> <br /> Also, what's the rule on which Spheres a Grimoire can raise? A level 5 Grimoire, how many Spheres can that raise for example? Is it all just ST caveat? So the Grimoire I'm thinking up is Paul's Letter to the Romans, torn from a cheap bible and reinforced for durability using Matter. Then the creator made notes on every bit of the letter in ballpoint pen and infused a tonne of Quintessence and layered in meditations on the nature of leadership, conscience, love, society etc.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking level 5, and it working for the Pattern Spheres (Life, Matter, Forces) as a reflection of the physical, and Mind and Correspondence to reflect how much the letter focuses on people and the connections between them. Would you accept a Grimoire with an Arete of 5 and 5 Spheres attached to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-07-2017, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T10:49:52-07:00","id":1125957,"title":"","content":"That would be...a pretty incredibly powerful Grimoire. As in, the Ascension War suddenly shifts as everyone fights to obtain it, because it's basically a multiple-degree master factory. Even if you accept the one-year-between-uses bit, that doesn't prevent multiple people from studying it every year. They can only get one dot of Arete from it, but still...<br /> <br /> IIRC there aren't a lot of examples of Grimoires in old Mage. So I don't have a good example to compare it against. <br /> <br /> Also, to your earlier question about the year delay - I think they were just looking for a rule that would keep Grimoires from being a Matrix-style &quot;upload-magick-powers&quot; thing. I agree you could come up with a more complex rule. Exmaple<br /> <br /> &quot;Each use of the Grimoire requires a certain period of study. Mages cannot concurrently study multiple things in Grimoires - their focus must be on grasping one concept at a time. If learning a new Ability, Knowledge, or Talent: the period is (new dot level) in weeks. If learning a Sphere level, the period is (new dot level) in months. If raising Arete, the period is one year. This period may not be avoided through mental acceleration or other Mind effects. Time effects to slow time for the student are effective, as are any Umbral realms where the passage of time is altered.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the times on that are more realistic, and they require studying for that amount of time rather than suddenly learning the thing and then having to spend X amount of time in the penalty box until you can go again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T11:13:43-07:00","id":1125963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125845-the-author-of-this-grimoire-goes-by-my-name?p=1125957#post1125957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be...a pretty incredibly powerful Grimoire. As in, the Ascension War suddenly shifts as everyone fights to obtain it, because it's basically a multiple-degree master factory. Even if you accept the one-year-between-uses bit, that doesn't prevent multiple people from studying it every year. They can only get one dot of Arete from it, but still...<br /> <br /> IIRC there aren't a lot of examples of Grimoires in old Mage. So I don't have a good example to compare it against.<br /> <br /> Also, to your earlier question about the year delay - I think they were just looking for a rule that would keep Grimoires from being a Matrix-style &quot;upload-magick-powers&quot; thing. I agree you could come up with a more complex rule. Exmaple<br /> <br /> &quot;Each use of the Grimoire requires a certain period of study. Mages cannot concurrently study multiple things in Grimoires - their focus must be on grasping one concept at a time. If learning a new Ability, Knowledge, or Talent: the period is (new dot level) in weeks. If learning a Sphere level, the period is (new dot level) in months. If raising Arete, the period is one year. This period may not be avoided through mental acceleration or other Mind effects. Time effects to slow time for the student are effective, as are any Umbral realms where the passage of time is altered.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the times on that are more realistic, and they require studying for that amount of time rather than suddenly learning the thing and then having to spend X amount of time in the penalty box until you can go again.</div> </div> </div> </div>- Really? For a very niche Grimoire? Firstly, if it's the letter to the Romans then you can ignore all Mages whose paradigms aren't based around Christianity. You're removing most Mages immediately. Then you're removing all of the ones whose paradigms don't match the liberal interpretation of Catholic dogma and tradition layered over it. You're removing ones who can't speak English, which is still kind of important. You're removing ones who fundamentally disagree with the annotations made in the sidelines; for example if it interprets &quot;use your own conscience guys&quot; (I'm paraphrasing as I'm sure you can guess) as &quot;you do you&quot; in terms of sexual conduct, MOST with a Christian paradigm just won't be able to internalize that, it runs contrary to a lot of religious lore and dogma. For the... 20 Mages who can use it? Really powerful. Now if it were a PRIMER too, now we're talking. Very accessible paradigm for young liberal Christians, which is a pretty huge % of the global population.<br /> <br /> - I like this, I personally would base how long it takes on rolls, make it so that you have to accumulate a certain number of successes on a sequence of rolls (Intelligence + Academics for a basic reading, Perception + Research to read around the topic, Wits + Esoterica to get that spark of inspiration while reflection, you do these three rolls in a sequence over and over until you hit X successes). Each roll is one Downtime. The difficulty is the Grimoire's level + 4, but this can be reduced by 1-3 using Sphere effects on a roll by roll basis. The number of successes needed is determined by the level of what you're learning. You can't spend Willpower on these rolls.<br /> <br /> - Abilities: 1 success per level<br /> - Arete: 5 successes per level<br /> - Affinity Sphere: 4 successes per level<br /> - Sphere: 5 successes per level<br /> <br /> So if you have a level 5 Grimoire and try and improve your Arete to 5 using it, you need to roll against Difficulty 9 until you accumulate 25 successes. Using Mind you can reduce the difficulty to 6, and then you just need to go at it until you succeed. Failures just do nothing and waste the downtime. Botches erase your progress and can inflict derangements, cost permanent Willpower etc. at storyteller discretion. More likely with a book of secrets stolen from demons than a book about friendly spirits.<br /> <br /> I like this since it makes low level Grimoires arguably more useful, especially for beginners. There's a reason to make a weak Grimoire; they're easier to learn from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T11:29:49-07:00","id":1125969,"title":"","content":"The successes method would work okay too - I just don't like rolling dice that frequently. Easier to abstract it as a flat amount of time.<br /> <br /> For the Grimoire - it sounds like you're assuming a Grimoire can only be used by those who completely align with the paradigm of the writer. I haven't heard that rule before, but you could certainly use it if you like. I will poke a few holes, though: language shouldn't be a barrier to anyone with Mind 3, and unless the Grimoire's creator is particularly annoying, it'd be easy for him/her to build that effect into it so it's universally readable. Also, if a Grimoire allows increasing Arete, in theory it grants insight into how paradigms are paradigms only and how a mage can appreciate multiple points of view / drop foci / etc. So it's at least partially a widening of perspective.<br /> <br /> For me I'd boil it down to what role I want Grimoires to play in the story. Are they primarily a method by which organized Traditions get their new recruits up to snuff - e.g., the new Hermetic gets a Grimoire copy of the <i>Corpus Hermeticum</i> and spends a year in the library? Then you want short study times, relatively weak dot levels available, and at least somewhat wide allowance for paradigms; any paradigm based in Hermetic theory should be fine with that Grimoire, not just the House Flambeau guys who can speak French. On the other hand, are Grimoires primarily Ancient Powerful MacGuffins, that unlock heretofore unknown secrets and are pursued by all? Then the paradigm bit should be split wide open - if everyone wants it, everyone should be able to use it - and long study times are fine, because when you finish you'll be incredibly powerful. <br /> <br /> Your approach of very powerful knowledge, very narrow paradigm, and very short study times just doesn't seem to align with any specific narrative role. It's not an object you'd compete with others over, since no one else can use it. It allows you to rapidly become very very powerful, which I'd only find useful to do offscreen as I transition from a story about neophytes to masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T12:07:49-07:00","id":1125983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125845-the-author-of-this-grimoire-goes-by-my-name?p=1125854#post1125854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Infuriatingly, someone with a lot of time on their hands has taken steps to eliminate all Time-related traces from the book. Not only has it been scrubbed clean of its history and past impressions made by those who have touched it, it seems to have been scrubbed clean of a temporal nature of any kind. Dating when it was published, and when the notes were made, seems impossible using Time Magick. Your Time-adept friend grows frustrated and gives the book back to you, surmising that someone with a mastery of Time superior to theirs has been very careful in covering their tracks.<br /> <br /> (Side Note I promise this isn't a &quot;aaaaaaaaaand you fail&quot; it's actually a sort of clue for my personal explanation, however I can think of three good ones)</div> </div> </div> </div>Once you go into &quot;and all traces have been wiped clear&quot;, you might as well assume that whoever handled the Grimoire also had Prime 2 and just changed the resonance to fuck with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T12:22:38-07:00","id":1125986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125845-the-author-of-this-grimoire-goes-by-my-name?p=1125983#post1125983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once you go into &quot;and all traces have been wiped clear&quot;, you might as well assume that whoever handled the Grimoire also had Prime 2 and just changed the resonance to fuck with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's a distinct possibility, but it leaves its own clues; someone knows your resonance well enough to imitate it very convincingly. That gives you a kind of lead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T12:32:20-07:00","id":1125990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125845-the-author-of-this-grimoire-goes-by-my-name?p=1125969#post1125969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The successes method would work okay too - I just don't like rolling dice that frequently. Easier to abstract it as a flat amount of time.<br /> <br /> For the Grimoire - it sounds like you're assuming a Grimoire can only be used by those who completely align with the paradigm of the writer. I haven't heard that rule before, but you could certainly use it if you like. I will poke a few holes, though: language shouldn't be a barrier to anyone with Mind 3, and unless the Grimoire's creator is particularly annoying, it'd be easy for him/her to build that effect into it so it's universally readable. Also, if a Grimoire allows increasing Arete, in theory it grants insight into how paradigms are paradigms only and how a mage can appreciate multiple points of view / drop foci / etc. So it's at least partially a widening of perspective.<br /> <br /> For me I'd boil it down to what role I want Grimoires to play in the story. Are they primarily a method by which organized Traditions get their new recruits up to snuff - e.g., the new Hermetic gets a Grimoire copy of the <i>Corpus Hermeticum</i> and spends a year in the library? Then you want short study times, relatively weak dot levels available, and at least somewhat wide allowance for paradigms; any paradigm based in Hermetic theory should be fine with that Grimoire, not just the House Flambeau guys who can speak French. On the other hand, are Grimoires primarily Ancient Powerful MacGuffins, that unlock heretofore unknown secrets and are pursued by all? Then the paradigm bit should be split wide open - if everyone wants it, everyone should be able to use it - and long study times are fine, because when you finish you'll be incredibly powerful.<br /> <br /> Your approach of very powerful knowledge, very narrow paradigm, and very short study times just doesn't seem to align with any specific narrative role. It's not an object you'd compete with others over, since no one else can use it. It allows you to rapidly become very very powerful, which I'd only find useful to do offscreen as I transition from a story about neophytes to masters.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't need to align perfectly, but you need to share a Paradigm. This specific Grimoire is Creation is Divine and Alive, with Christianity built into it. From what I've read of Grimoires it has to match your Paradigm in a broad sense, and you need to be compatible in terms of your beliefs about magic. This means that Grimoires are only really useful to huge numbers of people if they are very generic; for example there will be Grimoires that many Hermetics can use and there will be Grimoires that many Choristers can use, as these societies are built around having compatible paradigms for teamwork and study.<br /> <br /> As for everyone wanting Grimoires, a Mage could crave access to a Grimoire even if they can't use it. Firstly, it will still be worth reading and could teach you something about other people's methods of Magick. Secondly, you can use it as a bargaining chip with others, possibly make a trade. Last but not least, it's a Wonder and has magick built into its very being; that makes it valuable in and of itself.<br /> <br /> Take my hypothetical Letters to the Romans...<br /> <br /> Choristers: many would consider it profane, since it is provably powerful but has such a... deviant take on the words of the Apostles. Gods house may have many rooms, but do we want to give credence to such modern and disruptive interpretations of the Christ?<br /> <br /> Technocracy: a book that makes religious people into reality deviants? More than 2 Billion Catholics in the world makes this an awful thing that needs to be taken and neutralized.<br /> <br /> Cult of Ecstasy: &quot;now THIS is something I can get behind!&quot; - A Cultist hellbent on pissing off conservative religious Mages among the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Knights of the Temple of Solomon: &quot;HERESY!&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean it's far from world-changing, but many Mages have a reason to care, if only because it's making someone *else* rather powerful quite quickly. If you're a Hermetic, and proud of being such, and you see someone recently awakened breezing through Forces (not even their Affinity!) using a magical bit of pseudo-christian literature, you're going to be a tiny bit pissed off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}